---
code: tolerates-unknown-dimension
when-fires: an unknown context-dimension token appears on a `tolerates:` vouch. oracle/entry.rs collect_tolerance. `{expected}` = the known-dimension list.
why: 27C §2: the mark vouches nothing and the site stays walled on that dimension (engine-owned closed vocabulary).
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- tolerates-unknown-dimension && mise run loom:promote -- tolerates-unknown-dimension`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all tolerates-unknown-dimension` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
foo__is_converged() { foo "$@" : safe-across netns2; }

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  warning[tolerates-unknown-dimension]: sm `netns2` is not a known context
  dimension on a `tolerates:` vouch (expected one of user, fs-view, netns); the
  mark vouches nothing and the site stays walled on that dimension (`27C`
  section 2).
        [ oracle.sh:2:32
     2 | foo__is_converged() { foo "$@" : safe-across netns2; }
       |                                \__________________/

